3. SQL Joins
INNER JOIN: Connects two tables and shows only the matching records. It lists employees alongside their department names, skipping anyone without a department.

LEFT JOIN: Shows everything from the first (left) table and only matching data from the second. It lists every single department and its headcount—even departments that currently have 0 employees.

RIGHT JOIN: Shows everything from the second (right) table and only matching data from the first. It lists every office location and the staff working there, showing NULL (blank) for empty offices.


